Also fix the assembly formula to datasheet: value = (H<<6)|(L&0x3F), 14-bit two's complement. Update main loop:

```c
int16_t ax_raw = (int16_t)(((raw[1] & 0xFF) << 6) | (raw[0] & 0x3F));
```
Note (raw[1]<<6) with raw[1] up to 0xFF → 0x3FC0, sign: 14-bit two's complement — (H<<6)|(L&0x3F) gives a 14-bit unsigned; need sign extension: if bit13 set → subtract 0x4000. In C: int16_t v = (raw[1]<<6)|(raw[0]&0x3F); raw[1]<<6 as int = up to 16320+63 fits in int16 positive... if H=0xFF → 0x3FCF = 16335 > 32767? no fits. But the 14-bit value's bit13 = (H>>7)&1. Sign extend: if (v & 0x2000) v -= 0x4000.

Do:
```c
static inline int16_t qma14(uint8_t lsb, uint8_t msb) {
    int16_t v = (int16_t)(((msb & 0xFF) << 6) | (lsb & 0x3F));
    if (v & 0x2000) v -= 0x4000;
    return v;
}

