Confirmed. We have `httpd_req_async_handler_begin/complete`, `httpd_req_to_sockfd`, `httpd_socket_send`.

So the proper fix: make the stream handler async — hand off the request to a dedicated task, so the httpd main thread goes back to serving other requests.

Design:
- `stream_handler(req)`:
  - If a stream is already running (s_stream_busy flag), respond 503 quickly with a message, so extra clients don't pile up.
  - Else: `httpd_req_async_handler_begin(req, &async_req)`, get sockfd, set keepalive, spawn task (or wake an existing task) to write MJPEG frames with `httpd_socket_send`, then on exit call `httpd_req_async_handler_complete`.

Careful details:
- After async begin, must first send the response headers. `httpd_resp_set_type` etc. can be used on the async req before complete? Yes, the async req copy supports resp functions. But simpler: build and send the initial multipart header manually with `httpd_socket_send`.
- On completion: `httpd_req_async_handler_complete(async_req)` which closes the session properly.
- Must not exceed one async call at a time; there's a limit config `max_uri_handlers`? Actually `hd_calls` array sized by `CONFIG_HTTPD_ASYNC_HANDLERS`? Let me check: `hd->hd_calls = calloc(config->max_open_sockets, sizeof(...))`? From line 438: `free(hd->hd_calls)` — allocated somewhere. Let me check its size. Probably `config->max_open_sockets`. Fine.

Also enable `lru_purge_enable = true`, and set socket keepalive via `setsockopt(sockfd, SOL_SOCKET, SO_KEEPALIVE...)`. lwIP supports SO_KEEPALIVE if CONFIG_LWIP_TCP_KEEPALIVE. Need to enable in sdkconfig: `CONFIG_LWIP_TCP_KEEPALIVE=y`. Good idea to detect dead peers (e.g., when user sleeps laptop).

Also add a frame rate limiter: target ~10 fps to avoid flooding and to let WiFi breathe: `vTaskDelayUntil`. Actually better to push as fast as camera gives but add small delay when no new frame.

Additionally, IMU report interval 1s while camera streams: keep.

Another important improvement: the single-client policy — if a second browser opens the page, returning 503 immediately tells the page to retry later rather than hanging. The page will show a friendly message.

Let me now write the code.

Plan for camera_stream.c rewrite:
- Add `#include "lwip/sockets.h"`, `freertos/semphr.h`, `freertos/task.h`.
- globals: `static volatile bool s_stream_active = false;` and a TaskHandle.
- `stream_handler`:
```c
static esp_err_t stream_handler(httpd_req_t *req)
{
    httpd_req_t *async_req = NULL;
    if (s_stream_busy) {
        httpd_resp_set_type(req, "text/plain");
        httpd_resp_set_hdr(req, "Access-Control-Allow-Origin", "*");
        httpd_resp_set_status(req, "503 Service Unavailable");
        httpd_resp_send(req, "busy", HTTPD_RESP_USE_STRLEN); // careful with status APIs
        return ESP_OK;
    }
    esp_err_t err = httpd_req_async_handler_begin(req, &async_req);
    if (err != ESP_OK) { httpd_resp_send_err(req, HTTPD_500_INTERNAL_SERVER_ERROR, "async busy"); return ESP_FAIL; }
    // 启动/唤醒推流任务
    s_async_req = async_req;
    s_stream_busy = true;
    xTaskCreatePinnedToCore(stream_task, "cam_stream", 8192, NULL, 6, &s_task, 1);  // create per connection
    return ESP_OK;
}
```
Task:
```c
static void stream_task(void *arg) {
    httpd_req_t *req = (httpd_req_t*)arg;
    int sockfd = httpd_req_to_sockfd(req);
    enable keepalive
    // 发送 multipart 头
    httpd_socket_send(s_stream_httpd, sockfd, hdr, len, 0);
    loop:
      fb = esp_camera_fb_get();  // blocking
      ... send boundary, part header, frame ...
      if send fails -> break
      maybe check stop flag
    cleanup:
      httpd_req_async_handler_complete(req);
      s_stream_busy = false;
      vTaskDelete(NULL);
}
```
Careful: `esp_camera_fb_get()` blocks; when we want to stop, we can't easily. But we set a flag `Client disconnected` detection via send failure. Also set `send_wait_timeout` so sends return error rather than hanging forever. Actually `httpd_socket_send` uses `send()` with the configured `send_wait_timeout`? It uses `httpd_default_send` which sets SO_RCVTIMEO/SO_SNDTIMEO from config for that socket. With async handler from httpd, the socket has been configured already (httpd sets snd timeout on accept based on config.send_wait_timeout). Good: set `cfg.send_wait_timeout = 2` so a dead peer is detected within ~2s.

Hmm — careful: too short a send timeout might break slow-but-healthy clients. 3 seconds is reasonable.

Also, we should guard: if `esp_camera_fb_get()` returns NULL repeatedly, break.

Also add a max connection duration? Not needed.

